# Deployment Parameters File for Azure Developer CLI
# This file maps environment variables to Bicep parameters during deployment

# Generated by: Azure Preparation Specialist
# Date: 2026-03-19
# Purpose: AZD deployment parameter configuration

# ============================================================================
# ENVIRONMENT-TO-PARAMETER MAPPING
# ============================================================================

# These environment variables are automatically injected by AZD:
# - AZURE_CLIENT_ID (Managed Service Identity)
# - AZURE_TENANT_ID (Azure AD Tenant)
# - AZURE_SUBSCRIPTION_ID (Subscription ID)
# - AZURE_RESOURCE_GROUP (Resource Group Name)
# - AZURE_LOCATION (Region)

# ============================================================================
# SECRET PARAMETERS (Must be provided at runtime)
# ============================================================================

# databasePassword: Provided via environment variable or az keyvault secret get
# tinyFishApiKey: Provided via environment variable or az keyvault secret get
# jwtSecret: Provided via environment variable or az keyvault secret get
# sessionSecret: Provided via environment variable or az keyvault secret get

# ============================================================================
# DEPLOYMENT FLOW
# ============================================================================

# 1. AZD reads azure.yaml
# 2. AZD reads .azure/config.json for subscription/resource group
# 3. AZD packages services (builds Docker images)
# 4. AZD pushes images to Container Registry
# 5. AZD reads parameters from environment variables
# 6. AZD runs Bicep deployment with parameters
# 7. Bicep creates all Azure resources
# 8. AZD displays deployment outputs (URLs, endpoints)

# ============================================================================
# CUSTOM COMMAND EXAMPLES
# ============================================================================

# Deploy with custom parameters:
# azd deploy \
#   --parameter-file override.json \
#   --set databasePassword=${DATABASE_PASSWORD} \
#   --set appReplicas=3

# Deploy to production environment:
# azd env new production
# azd env set AZURE_LOCATION westus2
# azd up

# List all parameters:
# az deployment group create \
#   --template-file infra/main.bicep \
#   --what-if \
#   --parameters databasePassword=<password>
